---
# Warning baseline (OPE-4 "make CI signals honest and consistent"):
#
# Before this change, WarningsAsErrors was '' (empty), so clang-tidy never
# exited non-zero on its own -- every warning was purely informational
# regardless of what the CI wrapper scripts did with the exit code. That made
# the "clang-tidy lint" CI step decorative rather than a real gate.
#
# Measured backlog (local repro, see PR body for full methodology/caveats):
# scanning all ~250 project .cpp translation units with these Checks found
# 329 in-scope diagnostics across ~152 files (~61%). 292 of those 329 (89%)
# are a single check, readability-non-const-parameter, spread across ~116
# files -- almost all pre-existing, stylistic, and not something a partial
# CI pass should start hard-failing unrelated PRs over.
#
# clang-analyzer-* (the checks that actually indicate probable bugs --
# dead stores, calls on possibly-null/uninitialized values, virtual calls
# from constructors/destructors) is far more bounded: 26 findings across
# 19 files (~8% of the tree). That is a tractable, named backlog:
#   forms/control.cpp, framework/jukebox.cpp,
#   framework/sound/null_backend.cpp, framework/sound/sdlraw_backend.cpp,
#   game/state/battle/battleunit.cpp, game/state/city/agentmission.cpp,
#   game/state/city/building.cpp, game/state/city/city.cpp,
#   game/state/city/vehicle.cpp, game/state/gamestate.cpp,
#   game/state/shared/agent.cpp, game/state/tilemap/pathfinding.cpp,
#   game/state/tilemap/tileobject.cpp,
#   game/state/tilemap/tileobject_projectile.cpp,
#   game/ui/components/controlgenerator.cpp,
#   game/ui/general/messagelogscreen.cpp, game/ui/general/moreoptions.cpp,
#   game/ui/tileview/battletileview.cpp, game/ui/tileview/battleview.cpp
#
# Decision: promote clang-analyzer-* (plus hard compiler errors, which are
# clang-diagnostic-error) to WarningsAsErrors now -- a bounded, honest
# signal that will fail CI for genuinely-suspicious code without also
# failing every PR that happens to touch one of the ~60% of files carrying
# pre-existing readability-non-const-parameter debt. readability-non-const-
# parameter stays enabled (still visible in CI logs) but warn-only.
#
# Path to full enforcement: clean up the 19-file clang-analyzer list above,
# then work through the readability-non-const-parameter backlog file-by-file
# before adding it to WarningsAsErrors too.
Checks:          'clang-diagnostic-*,clang-analyzer-*,readability-non-const-parameter'
WarningsAsErrors: 'clang-diagnostic-error,clang-analyzer-*'
HeaderFileExtensions:
  - ''
  - h
  - hh
  - hpp
  - hxx
ImplementationFileExtensions:
  - c
  - cc
  - cpp
  - cxx
HeaderFilterRegex: 'forms/.*|framework/.*|game/.*|library/.*|tests/.*|tools/.*'
SystemHeaders:   false
...
